---

<DocsLayout
  title="Merge & Conflicts"
  description="Smart merge engine — semantic conflict resolution for .env, JSON, CSV, and TOML files."
  sidebarGroups={sidebarGroups}
  prevLink={{ href: '/docs/secrets/', label: 'Secrets' }}
  nextLink={{ href: '/docs/philosophy/', label: 'Philosophy' }}
>
  <h1>Smart Merge Engine</h1>
  <p>When multiple machines push changes, Git may produce merge conflicts. DaemonHound understands file <em>content</em> — not just raw text.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Engine identifies the file type</li>
    <li>Selects the appropriate merge driver</li>
    <li>Performs a <strong>3-way merge</strong> (base | local | remote)</li>
    <li>If a <strong>true conflict</strong> remains (same key changed), flags for manual resolution</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Merge drivers</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Driver</th><th>File types</th><th>Strategy</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>EnvDriver</strong></td><td><code>.env</code>, <code>.env.local</code></td><td>Key-value aware. Both sides modify same key = true conflict.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>JSONDriver</strong></td><td><code>.json</code></td><td>Structural merge at property level.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>CSVDriver</strong></td><td><code>.csv</code></td><td>Row-level merge.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>SecretDriver</strong></td><td>Secret TOML</td><td>Version-aware. Latest version wins.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>StateDriver</strong></td><td><code>state.toml.age</code></td><td>Vault state merge (highest priority).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>TextDriver</strong></td><td>Plaintext</td><td>Line-based fallback.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Example: .env merge</h2>
  <p>Machine A adds <code>STRIPE_KEY</code>, Machine B rotates <code>API_KEY</code>:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={`# Machine A added STRIPE_KEY
DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/mydb
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
API_KEY=sk-old
STRIPE_KEY=pk_test_a

# Machine B rotated API_KEY
DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/mydb
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
API_KEY=sk-new

# Smart merged result:
DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/mydb
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
API_KEY=sk-new
STRIPE_KEY=pk_test_a`} lang="Merge" />
  <p>Both changes apply cleanly — different keys. No manual intervention needed.</p>

  <h2>Resolving conflicts</h2>
  <h3>CLI</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={`dhd conflicts list
dhd conflicts show .env.local
dhd conflicts resolve .env.local --strategy local
dhd conflicts resolve .env.local --strategy remote
dhd conflicts clear`} />

  <h3>Web UI</h3>
  <p>Run <code>dhd ui</code> — 3-way diff view with side-by-side comparison.</p>

  <h3>Interactive TUI</h3>
  <CodeBlock code="dhd merge resolve" />

  <h2>Git integration</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={`dhd git setup      # Configure merge drivers, diff, filters
dhd git hook       # Install pre-commit, post-merge hooks`} />
</DocsLayout>
